    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0613" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg519"/>

                <head>No. 335.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                        West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 4th instant, accompanied by a copy of an approved report of
                    a committee of a privy council of Canada in relation to the cases of the
                    American fishing vessels <hi rendition="#italic">Pearl Nelson</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Everett Steele</hi> which were brought to your attention
                    by my notes of October 19th and 20th last.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
